    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output tonight, led by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who represent our strongest individual plays. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a favorable matchup against Quantrill, leveraging his elite .469 xwOBA to maximize production in a high-leverage spot. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a priority start, bolstered by a significant dynamic platoon edge (+14%) and a strong BvP history against Greene, making him an ideal candidate to capitalize on our league\u2019s premium on stolen base upside. Similarly, **Trea Turner** (69.64) provides stability from the leadoff spot; despite a slight platoon dip against Flaherty, his ability to manufacture runs and swipes keeps him as a cornerstone of the lineup.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, with **Caleb Durbin** (44.11) coming closest to breaking into the starting nine. While **Caleb Durbin** provides necessary speed, he was ultimately bypassed in favor of **Chase Meidroth** (57.50) and **Luke Raley** (55.02), both of whom benefit from substantially softer matchups against Lopez and Martinez, respectively. The optimizer prioritized the SP_xERA edge over **Caleb Durbin**\u2019s profile, given that our starting outfielders carry stronger combined platoon and park factors. \n\nRisks for the slate are relatively contained, though we are monitoring the bench status of **Christian Yelich**, who is out of commission due to a rainout. We are also keeping a close eye on **Kyle Schwarber** (60.84); while his xwOBA remains strong, his BvP history against Flaherty is concerning enough that he is being monitored for any early-game substitutions. The focus today remains on leveraging the speed of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Trea Turner** to maintain our competitive edge in the scarcest 5x5 category.",
